{# Only the narrow left column breaks a period over two lines. In the wide
   content column a period stays on one line, exactly as on the page. #}
{# The eyebrow of a section: the square marker and the label in grey
   capitals. The square is a drawn image, not a glyph and not a coloured cell –
   no embedded font is guaranteed to carry a filled square, and mPDF ignores a
   background on a block inside a table cell.

   NO SECTION NUMBER, unlike the page. Online the numbers structure one long
   scroll that has no table of contents; here there are four headings on two
   numbered pages and the ordinal earns nothing. It would also collide: "02"
   is Kompetenzen on the page and Selbstständigkeit in this document, so the
   same figure would mean two things across two documents that are meant to
   say the same. #}
{% macro eyebrow(title, markerPath) %}
    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0">
        <tr>
            <td width="5mm" valign="middle">
                <img src="{{ markerPath }}" style="width: 2mm; height: 2mm;">
            </td>
            <td valign="middle" class="eyebrow">{{ title }}</td>
        </tr>
    </table>
{% endmacro %}
{% macro period(years) %}
    {%- if ' – ' in years -%}
        {{ years|split(' – ')|first }} –<br>{{ years|split(' – ')|last }}
    {%- else -%}
        {{ years }}
    {%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}
{% import _self as parts %}
{# The printed curriculum vitae. Same content files as the page, different
   rendering – mPDF knows neither flexbox nor grid, so every column is a table
   cell and the rail beside the nested roles is a cell with one border.

   THE GRID, and everything lines up on it:

     20.0 mm   left margin
     30.5 mm   first column – half the logo width (61.03 ÷ 2)
     50.5 mm   text column starts here, in every section
    109.0 mm   the left column ends here – 20 mm of clearance follow
    129.0 mm   right column of the head, under the left edge of the logo
    190.0 mm   right margin

   Two typefaces, each with one job. Aller carries names, headings and every
   sentence; JetBrains Mono carries the technical layer – eyebrows, periods,
   locations, tags, labels and the dateline. Nothing mixes.

   This template holds literal hex values, which the interface templates must
   not: mPDF parses its own stylesheet and never sees the Tailwind theme, so
   there is no token to bind to. Same exception as `favicon.svg`. The values
   are the ones the tokens resolve to and have to move with them. #}
<style>
    /* TWO SCALES – five steps of type, four of spacing. Nothing in this
       document gets a size or a distance of its own; everything picks a step.

       TYPE
         24 pt  the title
         12 pt  the byline
         10 pt  names – a company, a role, a position
          9 pt  running text and values – the profile, the station
                descriptions, the contact column
          8 pt  the technical layer – periods, locations, competences and
                the labels in capitals

       The fifth type step earns its place. Names and running text shared one
       for a while; ten point for everything reads well and does not fit: the document ran to three pages, and the
       first ended at 168 mm because the Chefkoch block no longer had room
       beside the head. Nine point for the descriptions alone brings it back
       to two pages, so the extra step buys a whole page.

       SPACING – four steps, every distance a multiple of 1.5 mm
          0 mm  inside an entry, the lines sit flush – company, division,
                position, location; role and period. They are one unit, and
                the line height alone separates them, exactly as on the page.
        1.5 mm  between the rows of the contact column
        3.0 mm  between siblings – contact rows, profile paragraphs, stations
                within a section, roles under one employer, and a description
                under the line introducing it
        9.0 mm  between blocks – the title down to the profile, the head down
                to the first section, one section down to the next

       The one value off the scales is 0.5 mm above the period column: an
       optical nudge that puts the mono digits on the baseline of the company
       name beside them, not a distance between things.

       Every distance is padding on a table row or an explicit spacer element.
       mPDF drops block margins inside a table cell and renders an empty
       spacer only sometimes, so those are the two shapes that survive.

       This template holds literal hex values, which the interface templates
       must not: mPDF parses its own stylesheet and never sees the Tailwind
       theme, so there is no token to bind to. Same exception as
       `favicon.svg`. The values are the ones the tokens resolve to and have
       to move with them. */
    body { font-family: aller; font-size: 9pt; color: #525252; line-height: 1.45; }
    p { margin: 0; }

    h1 { font-family: aller; font-size: 24pt; font-weight: bold; color: #171717;
         margin: 0; letter-spacing: -0.5pt; line-height: 1.1; }
    .byline { font-family: aller; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold; color: #8200DB;
              margin: 0; }

    .eyebrow { font-family: jetbrainsmono; font-size: 8pt; letter-spacing: 1.6pt;
               text-transform: uppercase; color: #737373; }
    .rule { border-bottom-width: 0.25mm; border-bottom-style: solid;
            border-bottom-color: #E5E5E5; margin: 1.5mm 0 3mm 0; }

    .company { font-family: aller; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; color: #171717;
               line-height: 1.3; }
    .position { font-family: aller; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; color: #8200DB;
                line-height: 1.3; }
    .position-secondary { font-family: aller; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold;
                          color: #737373; line-height: 1.3; }

    .years { font-family: jetbrainsmono; font-size: 8pt; color: #737373; }
    .meta  { font-family: jetbrainsmono; font-size: 8pt; color: #737373; }
    .tags  { font-family: jetbrainsmono; font-size: 8pt; color: #737373; }
    .rail  { border-left-width: 0.25mm; border-left-style: solid; border-left-color: #E5E5E5; }

    .label { font-family: jetbrainsmono; font-size: 8pt; letter-spacing: 1.2pt;
             text-transform: uppercase; color: #737373; }
    .value { font-family: aller; font-size: 9pt; color: #171717; }
    .claim { font-family: aller; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; color: #171717; }
</style>

{# ── Kopf: Profil links, Kontakt unter der Logokante ───────────────────── #}
<table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0">
    <tr>
        <td width="89mm" valign="top">
            {# The whole left column is one table, one row per block. mPDF
               drops block margins inside a table cell and renders an empty
               spacer only sometimes; cell padding is the one thing it honours
               every time, so every vertical distance in this column is
               padding on a row. #}
            <table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0">
                <tr>
                    <td style="padding-bottom: 9mm;">
                        <h1>Lebenslauf</h1>
                        <p class="byline">von Marcel Kraus</p>
                    </td>
                </tr>
                {% for paragraph in profile %}
                    <tr><td style="padding-bottom: 3mm;">{{ paragraph }}</td></tr>
                {% endfor %}
                {# The claim closes the profile, as it closes the hero. Bold
                   rather than semi-bold: Aller is embedded in two weights and
                   a middle one does not exist to pick. #}
                <tr><td><span class="claim">{{ claim }}</span></td></tr>
            </table>
        </td>
        <td width="20mm"></td>
        <td width="61mm" valign="top">
            <table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0">
                {% for row in contact %}
                    <tr>
                        <td style="padding-bottom: 1.5mm;">
                            <p class="label">{{ row.label }}</p>
                            <p class="value">{{ row.value|raw }}</p>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                {% endfor %}
                <tr>
                    <td><img src="{{ qrCodePath }}" style="width: 18mm; height: 18mm;"></td>
                </tr>
            </table>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

{# Every vertical distance between blocks is a spacer of the same height, so
   the head sits as far from the first section as the sections sit from each
   other. A table margin would be right in a browser and is dropped here. #}
<div style="height: 9mm;"></div>

{# ── Stationen ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
{% for section in sections %}
    {% if section.milestones is not empty %}
        {% if loop.first == false %}<div style="height: 9mm;"></div>{% endif %}
        {{ parts.eyebrow(section.title, markerPath) }}
        <div class="rule"></div>

        {% for milestone in section.milestones %}
            <table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"
                   style="page-break-inside: avoid; margin-bottom: {{ loop.last ? '0' : '3mm' }};">
                <tr>
                    <td width="30.5mm" valign="top" style="padding-top: 0.5mm;">
                        <p class="years">{{ parts.period(milestone.years) }}</p>
                    </td>
                    <td valign="top">
                        {# One row per line, because a margin between them
                           would be dropped. The head of a station is tight
                           (1.5 mm), the description stands apart (3 mm). #}
                        <table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0">
                            <tr>
                                <td><span class="company">{{ milestone.company }}</span>{% if milestone.division is defined %}<br><span class="company">{{ milestone.division }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
                            </tr>
                            {% if milestone.position is defined %}
                                <tr>
                                    <td><span class="{{ milestone.marker|default('') == 'secondary' ? 'position-secondary' : 'position' }}">{{ milestone.position }}</span></td>
                                </tr>
                            {% endif %}
                            <tr>
                                <td class="meta" style="padding-bottom: {{ milestone.description is defined ? '3mm' : '0' }};">{{ milestone.location }}</td>
                            </tr>
                            {% if milestone.description is defined %}
                                <tr><td>{{ milestone.description }}</td></tr>
                            {% endif %}
                        </table>

                        {# One rail for all roles of an employer, not one per
                           role: the line is what says "these belong to the
                           company above", and a line with gaps in it says the
                           opposite. So the roles stack inside a single bordered
                           cell instead of each carrying its own. #}
                        {% if milestone.roles is defined %}
                            <table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="margin-top: 3mm;">
                                <tr>
                                    <td class="rail" width="5mm">&nbsp;</td>
                                    <td valign="top">
                                        <table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0">
                                            {% for role in milestone.roles %}
                                                <tr>
                                                    <td style="padding-bottom: {{ loop.last ? '0' : '3mm' }};">
                                                        <table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0">
                                                            <tr><td><span class="position">{{ role.position }}</span></td></tr>
                                                            <tr><td class="years" style="padding-bottom: {{ role.description is defined ? '3mm' : '0' }};">{{ role.years }}</td></tr>
                                                            {% if role.description is defined %}
                                                                <tr><td>{{ role.description }}</td></tr>
                                                            {% endif %}
                                                        </table>
                                                    </td>
                                                </tr>
                                            {% endfor %}
                                        </table>
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                            </table>
                        {% endif %}
                    </td>
                </tr>
            </table>
        {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{# ── Kompetenzen ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
<div style="height: 9mm;"></div>
{{ parts.eyebrow('Kompetenzen', markerPath) }}
<div class="rule"></div>

<table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="page-break-inside: avoid;">
    {% for group in skills %}
        <tr>
            <td width="30.5mm" valign="top" style="padding-bottom: 3mm;">
                <p class="label">{{ group.group }}</p>
            </td>
            <td valign="top" style="padding-bottom: 3mm;">
                <p class="tags">
                    {%- for entry in group.entries -%}
                        {{ entry.name }}{% if loop.last == false %}  ·  {% endif %}
                    {%- endfor -%}
                </p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    {% endfor %}
    <tr>
        <td width="30.5mm" valign="top"><p class="label">Fremdsprachen</p></td>
        <td valign="top"><p class="tags">{{ languages }}</p></td>
    </tr>
</table>

